should assess the possibility that circumcised men are compensating for decreased quality
of sexual experiences with increased variety and quantity.
Our respondents frequently commented that condoms were not an option for them due
to exacerbated loss of sensation. In two recent studies, Crosby confirmed that circumcised
men were significantly less likely than intact men to wear a condom when engaged in pen-
