Care.3
Large-scale
studies
of US
hospitals
indicate
that
most
male
infants
born
in
this
country
are
circum-
cised
in
the
newborn
period,4
although
the
circum-
cision
rate
recently
appears
to be decreasing.5
Since
the
1975
report,
new
evidence
has
suggested
possi-
ble
medical
benefits
from
newborn
circumcision.
Preliminary
data
suggest
the
incidence
of
urinary
tract
infection
in male
infants
may
be reduced
when
this
