and children for religious, societal or theoretical medical
beneﬁts. Although the amount of genital tissue removed
is variable, the penile prepuce is removed in nearly all
male circumcisions, and the clitoral prepuce is removed
in a Fourcroy grade 1 female circumcision [9] (see
Elchalal, pp. 103–108).
